  "i18n": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Domino Doodle",
      "concept": "The line you draw becomes a row of dominoes, and TOPPLE! sends them clattering along your own path. With branches, a limited supply and switch-opened gates, you design the order and length of the chain to ring every bell. Your layout survives a failed run, so tweaking and toppling again is the core loop.",
      "howToPlay": "Draw from the red-arrow domino to lay dominoes, then tap TOPPLE! to ring every bell. Start a line right beside a domino to branch.",
      "libraryDecision": "None. The game only needs a top-down chain rule (fall direction, reach, blocked by walls); matter-js is side-view 2D physics and cannot represent a path drawn on a tabletop, so a tiny custom chain simulation is both lighter and feels better.",
      "soundDecision": "No BGM. Each falling domino makes a short click whose pitch rises as the chain goes on, bells ring in a pentatonic scale, and switches thunk. The path you drew literally becomes a line of sound, so the chain itself is the music."
    }
  },
