    "i18n": {
      "en": {
        "comment": "Tracing a line that instantly becomes dominoes, then watching the rainbow chain clatter along and ring the bell, is genuinely satisfying. Corners and branches behave as they look, and on stage 5 the chain hit the closed gate first; adding one branch to the switch while keeping the layout fixed it, so the tweak-and-topple loop works. But the domino budgets are generous, so stages 1-4 pose little challenge and real puzzling only begins with the gates. Eight stages is short; volume and difficulty curve could go further.",
